hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"385","Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever swears by a surah from the Book of Allah, upon him is, for every verse of it, a binding oath; if he wishes he may fulfill it, and if he wishes he may break it."
"386","Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Razi narrated to us, 'Isa narrated to us, from 'Awf, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the same in meaning."
"387","Harun ibn 'Abbad al-Azdi narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Layth ibn Sa'd, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah and Rashid ibn Sa'd: A woman gave dates as a gift to 'A'ishah, and she ate some while some dates remained. The woman said: I adjure you to eat all of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The sin is upon the one who forces (another to break an oath)."
